{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:35-41,60-66,137-156` still honors `REBAR_HLC=0`, although `docs/remediation-implementation-plan.md:590-592` calls it a one-release rollback and many releases have since shipped. Disabling HLC can reintroduce causal ordering errors under skewed clocks. The removal also has load-bearing consumers beyond the HLC unit test: compaction concurrency scenarios used the switch for timestamp placement, and a seam guard counts its `# read-via:` marker.\n\n## Approach\n\nRemove `_enabled`, the `REBAR_HLC` environment read/registration, and the disabled raw-clock branch. Retain `REBAR_HLC_NOW` as the test-only physical-clock injection, legacy event reads, persisted-state locking, and deterministic clock tests.\n\nMigrate the two compaction integration scenarios without disabling HLC. Scenario A will build its far-past subject from the fresh clone that has no HLC cache, then use strictly ordered forward `REBAR_HLC_NOW` values for the young event, snapshot, and remote append; each tick is monotonic and the test proves the append sorts after the snapshot without a wall-clock race. Scenario B will create B’s below-snapshot orphan while B’s remote is disconnected and before B witnesses A’s future snapshot, using a valid injected future timestamp. After A publishes the higher future snapshot, reconnect B and drive a real engine write/push to merge and publish the pre-existing orphan; the test continues to prove detection and repair.\n\nUpdate all removal consumers: generated environment documentation, event-schema staging prose, the mechanism baseline, HLC unit tests, `test_store_paths` cleanup, the concurrency scenarios, and the held-out seam marker budget from 2 to 1. Add a focused exact-name sweep/oracle so `REBAR_HLC` cannot reappear while the distinct `REBAR_HLC_NOW` injection remains allowed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- HLC implementation and environment/deprecation registry\n- generated/operator and event-schema documentation plus the mechanism baseline\n- unit/store/integration/held-out consumers of the retired switch\n- a focused exact-name removal oracle\n\n## Testing\n\nRun the HLC unit suite, store-path test, both real push/fetch/merge compaction scenarios, the held-out snapshot-I/O seam guard, the environment-reference generator/check, lint, and typecheck. Use deterministic injected values and explicit cache/remote preconditions rather than wall-clock timing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The HLC implementation contains no `REBAR_HLC` disable branch or environment read; `REBAR_HLC_NOW` remains the sole test-time physical-clock override.\n- [ ] The live environment/deprecation registry, generated environment reference, `docs/event-schema.md`, and completed-remediation guidance no longer describe `REBAR_HLC=0`.\n- [ ] `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` no longer contains the retired `env_var::REBAR_HLC` mechanism entry.\n- [ ] Scenario A constructs its far-past ticket from a clone with an empty HLC cache and uses ordered forward injected clock values to prove the remote append sorts after the snapshot with HLC continuously enabled.\n- [ ] Scenario B writes its below-snapshot orphan while disconnected before it can witness A’s higher snapshot, then reconnects through a real engine write/push and still proves orphan detection plus snapshot repair.\n- [ ] `tests/scripts/test_store_snapshot_io_seam_clean_heldout.py` reduces `_store/hlc.py`'s marker budget from 2 to 1 when the retired read-via marker is removed.\n- [ ] HLC unit and store-path tests preserve legacy event readability, injected-clock behavior, and canonical HLC-state placement without setting or clearing `REBAR_HLC`.\n- [ ] A focused exact-name scan/test fails if `REBAR_HLC` is reintroduced outside the explicitly retained `REBAR_HLC_NOW` injection contract.\n- [ ] The HLC, store, concurrency, seam-guard, environment-reference, lint, and typecheck suites pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788376283589995001,"uuid":"dcbde3e5-9b7e-4db1-8a97-25c1b2197221"}